Article 16 These Provisions shall come into force as of the date of promulgation. The Provisions on the Labor Protection of Female Workers promulgated by the State Council on July 21, 1988 shall be abolished simultaneously.
Appendix:
Scope of Labor Prohibited for Female Workers
I. Scope of labor prohibited for female workers:
(1) Underground mining operations;
(2) Operations involving the fourth level of physical labor intensity as specified in the grading standard for physical labor intensity;
(3) Operations involving carrying loads more than six times per hour with each load exceeding 20 kilograms, or carrying loads intermittently with each load exceeding 25 kilograms.
II. Scope of labor prohibited for female workers during menstruation:
(1) Cold water operations of the second, third, and fourth levels as specified in the grading standard for cold water operations;
(2) Low-temperature operations of the second, third, and fourth levels as specified in the grading standard for low-temperature operations;
(3) Operations involving the third and fourth levels of physical labor intensity as specified in the grading standard for physical labor intensity;
(4) High-altitude operations of the third and fourth levels as specified in the grading standard for high-altitude operations.
III. Scope of labor prohibited for female workers during pregnancy:
(1) Operations in which the concentration of toxic substances such as lead and its compounds, mercury and its compounds, benzene, cadmium, beryllium, arsenic, cyanides, nitrogen oxides, carbon monoxide, carbon disulfide, chlorine, caprolactam, chloroprene, vinyl chloride, ethylene oxide, aniline, formaldehyde, etc., in the air of the workplace exceeds the national occupational health standards;
(2) Operations involving the production of anticancer drugs or diethylstilbestrol, or contact with anesthetic gases, etc.;
(3) Operations involving unsealed radioactive materials, or emergency response to nuclear accidents and radiation accidents;
(4) High-altitude operations as specified in the grading standard for high-altitude operations;
(5) Cold water operations as specified in the grading standard for cold water operations;
(6) Low-temperature operations as specified in the grading standard for low-temperature operations;
(7) Operations of the third and fourth levels as specified in the grading standard for high-temperature operations;
(8) Operations of the third and fourth levels as specified in the grading standard for noise operations;
(9) Operations involving the third and fourth levels of physical labor intensity as specified in the grading standard for physical labor intensity;
(10) Operations in confined spaces, high-pressure chambers, or diving operations, operations accompanied by strong vibration, or operations requiring frequent bending, climbing, or squatting.
IV. Scope of labor prohibited for female workers during breastfeeding:
(1) Items 1, 3, and 9 of the scope of labor prohibited during pregnancy;
(2) Operations in which the concentration of toxic substances such as manganese, fluorine, bromine, methanol, organophosphorus compounds, organochlorine compounds, etc., in the air of the workplace exceeds the national occupational health standards.
